# Panel 260 (provisional, author ratification pending): a group binding a
# function of the platform layer through a header of the program's own that
# declares it and includes none of the layer's headers. No group says
# `layer`, so the link carries none of the layer and misses the name; told at
# the group, before every other reader of a refused link, never as `internal
# error: linking failed` and never as a library no group names. The fix names
# the layer's header, which declares the function, and says the word.

extern "layer-a-name-of-the-layers-declared-by-a-header-of-the-programs-own.h"  #~ ffi_layer_undeclared
    function hero_time_monotonic_ns() -> i64

function main()
    print(hero_time_monotonic_ns() > 0)
